### Local MCP Server Run Methods in 3 Ways

###Method 1: Install (Traditional)**

###Install server once using npm.
#Example: 
npm install -g @modelcontextprotocol/server-github

#Method 2: npx (No installation): Uses Node.js to download and run the server temporarily.
#Example in config:
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-github"],
      "env": {
        "GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN": "<YOUR_TOKEN>"
      }
    }
  }
}
#Method 3: Docker (Containerized)** Runs MCP server inside a container using Docker.
#Example: docker run mcp/github-server

{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": {
      "command": "docker",
      "args": ["run", "-i", "--rm", "-e", "GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN", "mcp/github"],
      "env": {
        "GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN": "<YOUR_TOKEN>"
      }
    }
  }
}
